{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/outcomes-at-opening/packet-quality.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/outcomes-at-opening/packet-quality.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"item\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"What will the spot rental price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute average over calendar 2026, versus the roughly $3.20-an-hour peak reached in May 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The calendar-2026 average spot price for an hour of H100 GPU time on compute marketplaces, compared with the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026; settled by full-year 2026 H100 spot rental price data published after year-end 2026 (the quantity is for the current calendar year, per the item's 'over the last year' series).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The average spot price, in dollars per H100 GPU-hour, across calendar 2026, compared with the roughly $3.20/hour peak reported for May 2026.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $1.50 per H100 GPU-hour on average in calendar 2026, well below the ~$3.20 May 2026 peak\",\n   \"$1.50 to below $2.00 per H100 GPU-hour on average in calendar 2026, roughly half the May 2026 peak\",\n   \"$2.00 to below $2.50 per H100 GPU-hour on average in calendar 2026, moderately below the May 2026 peak\",\n   \"$2.50 to below $3.00 per H100 GPU-hour on average in calendar 2026, close to the May 2026 peak\",\n   \"$3.00 or above per H100 GPU-hour on average in calendar 2026, at or above the May 2026 peak\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 2,\n  \"description\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures be in calendar 2027?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined data-center capex (USD) of the four largest AI hyperscalers for calendar 2027.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; settled by the big four hyperscalers' full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their Q4/full-year 2027 earnings and SEC filings (early 2028), fixed by the release date of the annual figure.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined full-year 2027 data-center capital expenditures, in US dollars.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $850 billion\",\n   \"$850 billion to $950 billion\",\n   \"$950 billion to $1.05 trillion\",\n   \"$1.05 trillion to $1.2 trillion\",\n   \"Above $1.2 trillion\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 3,\n  \"description\": \"How much will U.S. federal agencies obligate in AI spending in 2026, versus the $7.2 billion reported as reached in 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The final total of U.S. federal AI spending obligations for 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026 (full-year 2026 data; check date 2026-12-31, set from the item's 2026 figure).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Full-year 2026 U.S. federal AI spending obligations as reported in federal procurement data (e.g., USAspending.gov) after 2026-12-31.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Less than $7.2 billion\",\n   \"$7.2 billion to less than $10 billion\",\n   \"$10 billion to less than $20 billion\",\n   \"$20 billion to less than $50 billion\",\n   \"$50 billion or more\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 4,\n  \"description\": \"What will the combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers — the customer pool that drives NVIDIA's data-center GPU demand — total?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Combined full-year 2026 capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers (the article puts the plan at around $650 billion for 'this year').\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026, full year ('this year' relative to the item's 4 July 2026 date); settled by the four hyperscalers' Q4 2026 earnings releases and 10-K filings in early 2027.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The combined calendar-2026 capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers, in US dollars, as reported in their full-year 2026 filings and Q4 2026 earnings releases.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Under $600 billion\",\n   \"$600 billion to under $650 billion\",\n   \"$650 billion to under $700 billion\",\n   \"$700 billion to under $750 billion\",\n   \"$750 billion or more\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 5,\n  \"description\": \"Will DRAM/HBM spot prices be higher or lower at the end of calendar 2026 than in mid-2026, after roughly tenfolding over the prior year as data-center memory demand outpaces supply?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in DRAM spot prices from mid-2026 to end-2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026-12-31 (end of calendar 2026; the check date for the change in DRAM spot price versus mid-2026).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The change in DRAM spot price from mid-2026 to end-2026.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Down more than 10%\",\n   \"Down 10% to up 10% (roughly flat)\",\n   \"Up more than 10% to 50%\",\n   \"Up more than 50% to 100%\",\n   \"More than double (up over 100%)\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 6,\n  \"description\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures be in calendar 2026 — the customer spending that underpins demand for Nvidia's data center GPUs?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined calendar-2026 data center capex of the big four AI hyperscalers, in US dollars, versus the ~$650 billion plan stated in mid-2026 and Nvidia's ~$1 trillion 2027 projection.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — set by the item's '$650 billion ... this year' plan figure (article dated 4 July 2026).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers, in US dollars.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $600 billion (below the ~$650 billion plan)\",\n   \"$600 billion to $650 billion (at or modestly below the ~$650 billion plan)\",\n   \"Over $650 billion up to $700 billion (at or modestly above the ~$650 billion plan)\",\n   \"Over $700 billion up to $750 billion (well above the ~$650 billion plan)\",\n   \"Over $750 billion (far above the ~$650 billion plan)\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 7,\n  \"description\": \"How much will NVIDIA have invested in Firmus Technologies, and what will its Firmus equity stake be carried at, at NVIDIA's next annual report, following its subscription for roughly $500 million of Firmus preference shares that convert to ordinary equity at Firmus's ASX IPO?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The dollar amount NVIDIA discloses as invested in Firmus Technologies and the carrying value of its resulting Firmus equity stake, versus the roughly $500 million subscription reported here.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA's next annual report (FY2027 Form 10-K, expected early 2027); the subscription is undertaken, so it is tracked by its amount at the next annual report.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The Firmus Technologies equity investment amount and carrying value NVIDIA discloses in its FY2027 Form 10-K (and interim 10-Q filings).\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"NVIDIA discloses less than $250 million invested in Firmus\",\n   \"NVIDIA discloses $250 million to less than $500 million invested in Firmus\",\n   \"NVIDIA discloses $500 million to less than $750 million invested in Firmus\",\n   \"NVIDIA discloses $750 million to less than $1.5 billion invested in Firmus\",\n   \"NVIDIA discloses $1.5 billion or more invested in Firmus\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 8,\n  \"description\": \"What will contract prices for DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X) and NAND memory do in calendar 2026, given AI-driven demand and tight supply that now put memory at 25–30% of Nvidia's Vera Rubin rack cost?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The year-over-year change in contract DRAM/LPDDR5X and NAND memory prices in calendar 2026 versus 2025.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (full year versus 2025) — set by the item: memory cost inflation and tight supply are reported as current drivers of 2026 rack prices, and no specific release date is given.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The 2026 year-over-year change in contract DRAM (DDR5/LPDDR5X) and NAND memory prices as published in memory-market contract price indices.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Contract memory prices fall year over year (change below 0%)\",\n   \"Contract memory prices rise 0% to 15% year over year\",\n   \"Contract memory prices rise 15% to 30% year over year\",\n   \"Contract memory prices rise 30% to 50% year over year\",\n   \"Contract memory prices rise more than 50% year over year\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 9,\n  \"description\": \"Where will US export-control policy on NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China stand at NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027 — will the US maintain the current conditional approval for some sales, broaden it, or re-tighten restrictions?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The state of US export-control permission for NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China as of NVIDIA's fiscal year-end 2027, as reflected in Commerce/BIS decisions and license approvals.\",\n  \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 (reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for an evolving regulatory stance the item reports as in force.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The US export-control status for NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China at the fiscal year-end check date: whether the current conditional approval is maintained unchanged, expanded, or withdrawn/re-tightened.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"US maintains the current conditional approval for NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China with no material change\",\n   \"US broadens approval, permitting additional NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China\",\n   \"US re-tightens, suspending or withdrawing the conditional approval for NVIDIA AI-chip sales to China\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 10,\n  \"description\": \"What will the spot rental price of an Nvidia H100 GPU-hour be in the fourth quarter of calendar 2026, after the roughly $3.20/hour peak in May 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The Q4 2026 average H100 GPU-hour spot rental rate on compute marketplaces such as Ornn, compared with the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak.\",\n  \"period\": \"Q4 calendar 2026; set from the item's 12-month H100 spot-price series published 2026-07-09, measured in Ornn's Q4 2026 data release (January 2027).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The Q4 2026 average spot rental rate for an Nvidia H100 GPU-hour in US dollars, compared with the ~$3.20/hour May 2026 peak reported in the item.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $1.00 per hour\",\n   \"$1.00 to under $1.75 per hour\",\n   \"$1.75 to under $2.50 per hour\",\n   \"$2.50 to under $3.10 per hour\",\n   \"$3.10 per hour or above (at or above the May 2026 peak)\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 11,\n  \"description\": \"Where will the spot price for an hour of H100-class GPU compute be at the end of calendar 2026, versus its ~$3.20/hour peak in May 2026, as custom AI accelerators from NVIDIA's largest customers pressure compute pricing?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The spot hourly rental price for an H100 GPU on compute marketplaces at end-2026, versus its May 2026 peak.\",\n  \"period\": \"2026-12-31 (end of calendar 2026; the check date for the spot H100 GPU-hour rate against its ~$3.20 May 2026 peak).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The spot price for an hour of H100 GPU compute at end-2026, measured against the ~$3.20/hour peak reported for May 2026.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $1.00 per GPU-hour\",\n   \"$1.00 to under $1.75 per GPU-hour\",\n   \"$1.75 to under $2.50 per GPU-hour\",\n   \"$2.50 to under $3.20 per GPU-hour\",\n   \"$3.20 per GPU-hour or above\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 12,\n  \"description\": \"How much will contract prices for the DRAM/DDR5 memory that dominates the bill of materials of AI server racks rise in calendar 2026, as tight DRAM, NAND and HBM supply meets AI-driven demand?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in contract DDR5 (DRAM) prices in calendar 2026 versus 2025, the memory input that now accounts for roughly a quarter or more of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack value.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 — checked against TrendForce/DRAMeXchange quarterly DRAM contract price data, with the Q4 2026 release settling the full-year change (release date fixes the check).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The year-over-year change in contract DDR5 (DRAM) prices for calendar 2026 versus calendar 2025, as published in quarterly contract price surveys (TrendForce/DRAMeXchange).\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Contract DDR5 prices fall on average in 2026 versus 2025\",\n   \"Contract DDR5 prices rise 0–20% in 2026 versus 2025\",\n   \"Contract DDR5 prices rise 20–40% in 2026 versus 2025\",\n   \"Contract DDR5 prices rise 40–80% in 2026 versus 2025\",\n   \"Contract DDR5 prices rise more than 80% in 2026 versus 2025\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 13,\n  \"description\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend in total on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Combined calendar-2027 data center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers, as disclosed in their quarterly and annual filings.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027; checked by 2028-03-31, after the four hyperscalers report Q4 2027 results and file their 2027 10-Ks.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The combined calendar-2027 data center capital expenditure total of the big four AI hyperscalers, taken from their reported capex disclosures and full-year guidance.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $700 billion\",\n   \"At least $700 billion but below $850 billion\",\n   \"At least $850 billion but below $1,000 billion\",\n   \"At least $1,000 billion but below $1,150 billion\",\n   \"At least $1,150 billion\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 14,\n  \"description\": \"Will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027 reach the $1 trillion that NVIDIA projects?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Aggregate calendar-2027 data-center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers, summed from their quarterly reports.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar year 2027; check date 2028-02-15, set because the item's projection is for 'next year' (2027) and full-year totals are only known once the four hyperscalers report fourth-quarter 2027 results.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Combined calendar-2027 data-center capital expenditures of the big four AI hyperscalers, summed from their quarterly earnings reports and capital-expenditure disclosures.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $750 billion\",\n   \"$750 billion to $900 billion\",\n   \"$900 billion to $1.0 trillion (below but approaching NVIDIA's $1 trillion projection)\",\n   \"$1.0 trillion to $1.15 trillion (meets NVIDIA's $1 trillion projection)\",\n   \"Above $1.15 trillion\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 15,\n  \"description\": \"What will the industry average contract price of DRAM (including high-bandwidth memory) be in calendar 2027, the memory input now making up roughly 25–30% of an Nvidia Vera Rubin rack's bill of materials?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The average contract price of DRAM/HBM memory in calendar 2027 versus 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 (the item's 'next two years' / next calendar year from its mid-2026 date).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The average contract price of DRAM/HBM memory in calendar 2027, expressed as its change against the 2026 average.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Down more than 10% versus 2026\",\n   \"Down 10% or less (through flat) versus 2026\",\n   \"Up more than 0% but under 10% versus 2026\",\n   \"Up 10% to under 25% versus 2026\",\n   \"Up 25% or more versus 2026\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 16,\n  \"description\": \"What share of Chinese companies' AI accelerator budget will go to domestic products over the 12 months following the July 2026 Bloomberg Intelligence survey, versus executives' planned 46% (up from 30%)?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"Domestic suppliers' realized share of surveyed Chinese companies' AI accelerator budget allocations over the 12 months from July 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"12 months from the July 2026 survey (to about July 2027); settled by a follow-up survey or China AI accelerator market-share data released around mid-2027.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The share of Chinese companies' AI accelerator budget allocated to domestic products over the 12 months from July 2026, measured against the ~30% current and 46% planned levels.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below 30% (domestic share falls below the current level)\",\n   \"30% to below 38% (little progress from the current level)\",\n   \"38% to below 46% (progress but short of the plan)\",\n   \"46% to below 55% (at or modestly above plan)\",\n   \"55% or above (well above plan)\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 17,\n  \"description\": \"What will the combined data center capital expenditure of the big four AI hyperscalers be in calendar 2027, versus the ~$650 billion they plan to spend in 2026 and Nvidia's projection that the figure could reach ~$1 trillion?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The combined 2027 data center capex of the four largest AI hyperscalers, in dollars, measured against the ~$650 billion 2026 plan and Nvidia's ~$1 trillion projection for 2027 — the demand pool that underpins Nvidia's data center revenue.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 — set by the item: Nvidia projects hyperscaler data center capex could reach $1 trillion 'next year' in an article dated 4 July 2026.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"Combined calendar-2027 capital expenditure on data centers disclosed by the four largest AI hyperscalers in their Q4 2027 earnings releases and Form 10-K cash-flow/capex disclosures (published early 2028), compared with the ~$650 billion planned for 2026 and Nvidia's ~$1 trillion projection.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $700 billion\",\n   \"$700 billion to $850 billion\",\n   \"$850 billion to $950 billion (below Nvidia's ~$1 trillion projection but well above the ~$650 billion 2026 level)\",\n   \"$950 billion to $1.05 trillion\",\n   \"Above $1.05 trillion\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 18,\n  \"description\": \"What will the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures be in calendar 2026 — the spending pool that drives demand for NVIDIA's data-center GPUs?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' combined reported data-center capital expenditures for calendar 2026.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2026 (full year); checkable when the big four hyperscalers report Q4 2026 results in early 2027. Set as the quantity (several companies' combined spending) for this calendar year under the shared-quantity rule.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The big four AI hyperscalers' aggregate reported data-center capital expenditures for calendar 2026, aggregated from their quarterly and full-year disclosures.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Less than $550 billion\",\n   \"$550 billion to less than $600 billion\",\n   \"$600 billion to less than $650 billion\",\n   \"$650 billion to less than $700 billion\",\n   \"$700 billion or more\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 19,\n  \"description\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The four largest AI hyperscalers' combined full-year 2026 data center capital expenditures, as reported in their filings.\",\n  \"period\": \"Full-year calendar 2026 ('this year' in the 2026-07-04 item); settled by the four companies' full-year 2026 capex disclosures in early 2027.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The four largest AI hyperscalers' combined full-year 2026 data center capital expenditures, compared with the ~$650 billion plan the item cites.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Below $550 billion\",\n   \"$550 billion to $624 billion\",\n   \"$625 billion to $674 billion\",\n   \"$675 billion to $749 billion\",\n   \"$750 billion or more\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 20,\n  \"description\": \"What will DRAM and high-bandwidth memory prices be at the end of calendar 2026, after memory makers raised prices roughly tenfold over the year to July 2026?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The year-on-year change in the DRAM/HBM price in Q4 calendar 2026 versus Q4 2025.\",\n  \"period\": \"Q4 calendar 2026; set from the item's 12-month memory-price series published 2026-07-09, measured in the Q4 2026 price releases published in early 2027.\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The year-on-year percentage change in the Q4 2026 DRAM/HBM price versus Q4 2025, as published by TrendForce/DRAMeXchange and the Datatrack DRAM spot price series cited in the item.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"More than 100% higher than a year earlier\",\n   \"50% to 100% higher\",\n   \"20% to under 50% higher\",\n   \"Up to 20% higher (including flat)\",\n   \"Lower than a year earlier\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 21,\n  \"description\": \"Will contract prices for server DRAM (DDR5/next-generation memory) keep rising through calendar 2027, raising the memory cost embedded in NVIDIA's Vera Rubin AI racks — now 25–30% of the bill of materials — and so pressuring system margins or rack prices?\",\n  \"outcome\": \"The change in average contract prices for server DRAM in calendar 2027 versus calendar 2026, as published by contract-price trackers or disclosed by memory makers.\",\n  \"period\": \"Calendar 2027 versus calendar 2026: set by the reason (a shared quantity for this or next calendar year, from the item's 6 July 2026 date).\",\n  \"settles_on\": \"The year-on-year change in average contract DDR5 server DRAM prices in calendar 2027, from published contract price surveys (e.g. TrendForce) or memory makers' disclosed contract pricing.\",\n  \"outcomes\": [\n   \"Average contract DDR5 server DRAM price in calendar 2027 falls more than 20% versus calendar 2026\",\n   \"Average contract DDR5 server DRAM price in calendar 2027 falls by 0–20% versus calendar 2026\",\n   \"Average contract DDR5 server DRAM price in calendar 2027 rises by more than 0% but at most 25% versus calendar 2026\",\n   \"Average contract DDR5 server DRAM price in calendar 2027 rises by more than 25% but at most 75% versus calendar 2026\",\n   \"Average contract DDR5 server DRAM price in calendar 2027 rises by more than 75% versus calendar 2026\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 12 '结果档可核对|中间一档|标的问题的档' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 12 '结果档可核对|中间一档|标的问题的档' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"292-<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n293-<ul>\n294-<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n295-<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n296-<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n297-<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n298-</ul>\n299-\n300-<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n301-<ul>\n302-<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n303-<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n304:<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n305-<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n306-</ul>\n307-\n308-<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n309-<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n310-<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n311-<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n312-\n313-<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n314-<ol class=\"steps\">\n315-<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n316-<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '245,293p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '245,293p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>词</th><th>意思</th><th>不要和它混</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">陈述</td><td>原文里某一方说的一句话或一件事</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">证据</td><td>被留下的陈述，带引文、摘要、说话人、原始出处、来源层</td><td>作者的观点（它本身可以是一条证据）</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">问题（观点）</td><td>账本里追踪的一件事：一个问题句、一组结果档、一个到期日，写下后不改<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">候选问题</td><td>抽取这一步提议新开的问题</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">标的问题、主题问题</td><td>标的：答案是一家可交易公司（或币、商品）自己的经营结果。主题：答案是世界上的一件事，影响很多公司<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">结果档</td><td>一个问题事先固定、互不重叠、覆盖全部结果的结局，五档或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 rung</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">来源层</td><td>事实、当事人陈述、第三方观点、传闻<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 evidence tier</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">分量</td><td>一条证据对判断有多重要：核心、辅助、可选、不收<span class=\"src\">第 6 节；D243</span>。Alex 说的\"档位低一点\"指它</td><td>结果档、来源层</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究用途</td><td>判断这一步引用一条证据去支持一个具体结论时，它撑得住多强：直接可用、有条件可用、线索、不可用<span class=\"src\">D221，第 7 节</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">七类驱动</td><td>一条陈述为什么对公司业务重要的七条路径<span class=\"src\">D208</span>。需求：客户要买多少，如订单、客户支出、贷款需求、客流。供给与投入：能做出多少、成本多少，如产能、原料和零部件价格、燃料、矿石品位。竞争与份额：对手的产品、价格、开店、赢单。定价与装机：公司能收多少价、存量多大，如售价、费率、利差、装机量、存量客户。产品周期：发布、出货、试验、获批、延期。政策：法规、许可、关税、利率、监管决定。资本与义务：融资、担保、承诺、投资、收购</td><td>问题类型</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">市场预期与估值</td><td>市场已经定价了什么：估值倍数、市值、目标价、股价反应。观点的立场要和它比<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。对一个业务量的一致预期（收入、EPS）是那个业务量的证据，不归这里</td><td>七类驱动</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究组</td><td>几个问题共同在追的一件正在进行的事<span class=\"src\">D165</span></td><td>问题</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本里记三种东西</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>证据</b>一条记录一个陈述，一件事用几句话说仍是一条<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；Alex 判 11</span>。记逐字引文、能单独读懂的一句话摘要、说话人、原始说话人和原始日期（不知道就写不知道，不填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>）、来源层。同一条证据可以挂到几个问题上，推力写在挂接上<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。每一条进来的证据都单独存下；和已有证据的关系（同一说法、修订）由匹配标出，作为意见，两条都留着<span class=\"src\">D202、D204</span>。原始说话人、原始日期、数字都相同的几条（说话人或日期不知道的不算相同），由代码认作同一条：判断时只给看一次，写明几家报道，每条仍照存<span class=\"src\">D248 第 7 条；改 D204 的\"两条都给判断看\"</span>。这条在打开之前要先在同一说法的金标上量两件事（金标按这条规则实际会合的组取，对着原文读）：它会不会藏掉不同或更丰富的说法（比如多一句限定），它依赖的原始说话人、原始日期两个字段准不准；量完之前，照 D204 两条都给判断看。</li>\n<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":1,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"f\"],\"why\":\"The top outcome says $3.00 is at or above the roughly $3.20 peak, although values below $3.20 are lower.\"}\n{\"item\":2,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"c\",\"d\"],\"why\":\"Adjacent ranges overlap at $950 billion, $1.05 trillion and $1.2 trillion. The middle range gives no comparison baseline.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline. Full-year data published after December 31 cannot settle the question on that check date.\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline.\"}\n{\"item\":5,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"b\",\"d\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The price series and mid-2026 reference date are unspecified. The middle range omits its comparison, and the outcomes omit HBM.\"}\n{\"item\":6,\"pass\":\"yes\",\"failed\":[],\"why\":\"The ranges cover the amount without overlap, and the middle outcome compares it with the stated plan.\"}\n{\"item\":7,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline. The outcomes measure the investment amount but omit the separately requested carrying value.\"}\n{\"item\":8,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"b\",\"c\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"DRAM, LPDDR5X and NAND can move differently, with no aggregation specified. The ranges also overlap at 15% and 30%.\"}\n{\"item\":9,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"],\"why\":\"There are three event outcomes. 'Material change' is undefined, and simultaneous expansion and tightening or partial changes do not fit cleanly.\"}\n{\"item\":10,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline. The top range calls $3.10 at or above a roughly $3.20 peak.\"}\n{\"item\":11,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline.\"}\n{\"item\":12,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"c\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The ranges overlap at 20%, 40% and 80%. A Q4 release alone does not necessarily establish the full-year average change.\"}\n{\"item\":13,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline. Full-year guidance does not establish actual spending.\"}\n{\"item\":14,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"a\",\"c\"],\"why\":\"The question is yes/no but has five outcomes. Adjacent ranges overlap, including at the $1 trillion threshold.\"}\n{\"item\":15,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"b\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"DRAM and HBM have different prices; no product mix or averaging method defines the single price or its change.\"}\n{\"item\":16,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"e\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The theme outcomes call increases 'progress.' Market share is not necessarily the surveyed companies' budget allocation.\"}\n{\"item\":17,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"c\"],\"why\":\"Adjacent ranges overlap at $700 billion, $850 billion, $950 billion and $1.05 trillion.\"}\n{\"item\":18,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"d\"],\"why\":\"The middle range gives no comparison baseline.\"}\n{\"item\":19,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"c\",\"d\"],\"why\":\"Values between $624 billion and $625 billion, and between other adjacent whole-billion endpoints, are uncovered. The middle range lacks a comparison.\"}\n{\"item\":20,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"b\",\"c\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"DRAM and HBM series have no specified aggregation; 20% belongs to two outcomes. A year-on-year change does not give the end-2026 price.\"}\n{\"item\":21,\"pass\":\"no\",\"failed\":[\"a\",\"f\"],\"why\":\"The question asks whether prices keep rising, but has five quantity outcomes. An annual average increase cannot establish a continuous rise.\"}"}}
